<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greeks</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greeks are a people of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> whose language and culture spread widely through colonisation, trade and conquest. They feature in the histories of many empires: as adversaries of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>, as the ruling elite of the Macedonian, Ptolemaic and Seleucid empires, and as the core population of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. Greek learning was later translated and preserved under the Umayyad and Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a>.</p></div>
